# Prerequisites
*.d

# Compiled Object files
*.slo
*.lo
*.o
*.obj

# Precompiled Headers
*.gch
*.pch

# Compiled Dynamic libraries
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll

# Fortran module files
*.mod
*.smod

# Compiled Static libraries
*.lai
*.la
*.a
*.lib

# Executables
*.exe
*.out
*.app

# CMake build output.
#
# build_*/ as well as build-*/: the hyphen form was covered and the UNDERSCORE
# form was not, so build_macos/ and smaragd/build_macos/ were tracked from
# 2026-06-02 to 2026-10-05 -- 83 generated files, every one of them Qt moc
# autogen, ninja state or CMake internals.
#
# The per-file rules below are NOT a substitute, and that is the whole point of
# this pattern. They catch most of a build tree incidentally (CMakeFiles/, *.d,
# *.a), which is why the leak looked harmless, but nothing here matched
# tw303a_autogen/moc_predefs.h, mocs_compilation.cpp or timestamp -- so those
# came back as untracked-and-unignored after every build, one `git add -A` away
# from being committed again. Untracking them (#219) did not close that; only a
# directory rule does.
#
# The trailing slash matters: it keeps smaragd/tw303a/sidecar/tools/
# build_body_probe.sh (a tracked script, see the note further down) out of the
# match. The same gap in nassau-mangrove2 kept build_phase5/ and build_vst3/ in
# that repo's history (QBX-132).
build/
build-*/
build_*/
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
CTestTestfile.cmake
Testing/
_deps/
compile_commands.json

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user

# clangd's index. A language server writes it beside the source it indexes, so
# it appears wherever someone runs one and is never a build product -- no
# per-file rule above would catch the .idx files. Listed here before it exists
# in this repo rather than after: nassau-mangrove2 had 172 of them untracked
# and unignored (nassau-mangrove2#10), and a pattern added once a directory is
# already tracked does nothing.
.cache/

# Local git worktrees (never track as gitlinks)
.claude/worktrees/

# qxa test artifacts. Everything under test-output/ is REGENERATED by every
# suite run (renders, and screenshots that capture the whole desktop because
# the screenshot action grabs the root window, not the app window). Two such
# desktop captures reached the remote before this rule existed.
smaragd/test-output/

# Steinberg ASIO SDK — licensed, NOT redistributable (unlike the clap/vst3
# submodules), so it is a manual drop-in: unzip the SDK from steinberg.net to
# smaragd/third_party/asiosdk. It must never be committed.
smaragd/third_party/asiosdk/
# Hand-made scratch audio at the repo root. Named individually ON PURPOSE: a
# blanket *.wav / *.ogg would also match render.wav and test_sawtooth.wav, which
# ARE tracked here and are fixtures the qxa cases depend on.
/testspur.wav
/testspur.ogg

# The proposal 44 verification probe, built at the repo root by
# smaragd/tw303a/sidecar/tools/build_body_probe.sh. A BINARY, and it was
# committed once by an over-broad `git add -A` before this line existed.
/body_probe

# thinktank: generated briefing and your own Claude Code memory (CYB-219)
.claude/thinktank-briefing.md
CLAUDE.local.md
